{"n": 258, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "258.webp", "text": "2113096\n\n1351... CHECKING ATMOSPHERIC\n\nPRESSURE DEPENDENT\nREGULATION\n\n1) Leak Test on Diaphragm:\n\nPlug hose (5a).\n\nConnect vacuum pump on connection (4)\nand produce 300 to 350 mbar vacuum.\nPulling off the hose on connection (4) will\ncause pressure pin (12) to move up suddenly\nagainst adjusting screw (11).\n\nThis is indicated by a loud click.\n\nIf diaphragm (10) leaks, the regulation will\nnot work and the injection pump has to be\nreplaced.\n\n2) Function of Control Unit:\n\nControl unit (5) holds the pressure underneath\ndiaphragm (10) at a constant value* continu-\nously.\n\nExample:\n\nAbsolute air pressure 980 mbar\nPressure measured in line 5a —_270 mbar\nConstant absolute pressu 710 mbar\nundefneath diaphragm\n\nThe vacuum measured in line (Sa) will always\ndepend on the absolute air pressure.\nConstant Pressure* Not Reached:\nCheck lines for leaks.\n\nCheck flow in filter.\n\nReplace control unit, if necessary.\n\n* See Specifications\n\n=\n‘ 2013 198\n4\n\n1 Fuel feed\n\n2 Fuel return\n\n3 Venting (cap must be unscrewed)\n4 Vacuum supply > 300. mbar)\n\n5 Control unit\n\n6 Elbow hose (must face down)\n\n7 Filter (check direction of flow)\n8 Orifice\n\n9 Vacuum pump", "words": [["2113096", 0.1662, 0.5312, 0.2062, 0.5411], ["1351...", 0.2639, 0.0637, 0.3095, 0.0756], ["CHECKING", 0.3252, 0.0637, 0.383, 0.0756], ["ATMOSPHERIC", 0.3865, 0.0637, 0.4661, 0.0756], ["PRESSURE", 0.3252, 0.0796, 0.3815, 0.0915], ["DEPENDENT", 0.3855, 0.0802, 0.4524, 0.0915], ["REGULATION", 0.3257, 0.0962, 0.3992, 0.1081], ["1)", 0.2639, 0.128, 0.2725, 0.1412], ["Leak", 0.2776, 0.1253, 0.2989, 0.1459], ["Test", 0.3034, 0.1253, 0.3237, 0.1459], ["on", 0.3283, 0.1253, 0.3394, 0.1459], ["Diaphragm:", 0.343, 0.128, 0.3977, 0.1426], ["Plug", 0.2614, 0.1406, 0.2832, 0.1631], ["hose", 0.2872, 0.1406, 0.3075, 0.1631], ["(5a).", 0.3121, 0.1406, 0.3343, 0.1631], ["Connect", 0.2614, 0.1572, 0.3024, 0.1777], ["vacuum", 0.